<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- The five troughs of "Alpha Props - Parks and Gardens" (sarg.alphapropsparks) become
       animal feeders.

       WHAT THEY ARE TODAY: five one-tile boxes labelled "trough", with isInert, WorkToBuild 0
       and no cost. The game has no feeder of any kind - hay is dumped on the floor of a barn and
       rots there - so the one prop that is literally shaped for the job does nothing.

       WHY Building_Storage AND NOT A STOCKPILE ZONE. Both work. A zone painted over the tile
       would have needed only surfaceType, and would have cost nothing. Building_Storage was
       chosen because it carries the storage tab: without a filter the trough would accept
       whatever the barn stockpile accepts, and a "feeder" that fills with steel is not a feeder.
       preventDeteriorationOnTop is the second reason, and the one that changes play: hay in a
       trough no longer rots in the rain, so the trough can stand outdoors in the pasture where
       the animals actually are.

       ANIMALS CAN REACH IT. The troughs are PassThroughOnly with fillPercent 0.5 - an animal
       walks onto the tile. That is what matters for eating, not the storage class: food-seeking
       resolves through ClosestTouch, and a passable tile is touchable. This is the same reason
       animals raid shelves.

       THE PRICE OF THE CONVERSION, AND WHAT REPLACES IT. These props inherit
       VFEProps.Building_SubstractsSilver, the class that charges silver at build time in place of
       a costList. thingClass is a single field: taking Building_Storage gives that up, and the
       troughs would otherwise become free. They are given 25 wood and WorkToBuild 400 instead -
       cheaper than a shelf, which is 20 stuff and 500 work but behind research.

       ALL FIVE, NOT JUST THE TWO SENSIBLE ONES. The empty trough and the hay trough are the
       obvious feeders; the three flower ones are planters by texture. They are converted all the
       same, because the alternative is to leave three pure props standing - and a prop that stays
       a prop is exactly what this mod exists to refuse. One function, five looks. Hay stored in a
       flower trough will draw on top of the flowers.

       THE FILTER IS WIDER THAN THE DEFAULT. Fixed settings allow the whole Foods category, so a
       player who wants to hand-feed meals to a bonded animal can. Defaults ship hay and kibble
       only, which is what a trough is for. Note that hay and kibble sit directly under Foods in
       vanilla, not under FoodRaw - filtering on FoodRaw would have excluded both.

       GUARD: one PatchOperationConditional per trough, each testing its own def. -->

  <!-- ================================= empty trough (AP_EmptyTrough) ================================= -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AP_EmptyTrough"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AP_EmptyTrough"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <thingClass>Building_Storage</thingClass>
            <surfaceType>Item</surfaceType>
            <canOverlapZones>false</canOverlapZones>
            <inspectorTabs>
              <li>ITab_Storage</li>
            </inspectorTabs>
            <costList>
              <WoodLog>25</WoodLog>
            </costList>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AP_EmptyTrough"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>A feeding trough. Animals eat directly from it, and food stored inside does not deteriorate, so it can stand out in the open.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AP_EmptyTrough"]/statBases/WorkToBuild</xpath>
          <value>
            <WorkToBuild>400</WorkToBuild>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AP_EmptyTrough"]/building</xpath>
          <value>
            <storageGroupTag>PIU_Trough</storageGroupTag>
            <maxItemsInCell>3</maxItemsInCell>
            <preventDeteriorationOnTop>true</preventDeteriorationOnTop>
            <ignoreStoredThingsBeauty>true</ignoreStoredThingsBeauty>
            <blueprintClass>Blueprint_Storage</blueprintClass>
            <fixedStorageSettings>
              <filter>
                <disallowNotEverStorable>true</disallowNotEverStorable>
                <categories>
                  <li>Foods</li>
                </categories>
              </filter>
            </fixedStorageSettings>
            <defaultStorageSettings>
              <priority>Normal</priority>
              <filter>
                <thingDefs>
                  <li>Hay</li>
                  <li>Kibble</li>
                </thingDefs>
              </filter>
            </defaultStorageSettings>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

